;b.getElementsByTagName('head')[0].appendChild(d)}}if(document.body){var a=document.createElement('iframe');a.height=1;a.width=1;a.style.position='absolute';a.style.top=0;a.style.left=0;a.style.border='none';a.style.visibility='hidden';document.body.appendChild(a);if('loading'!==document.readyState)c();else if(window.addEventListener)document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',c);else{var e=document.onreadystatechange||function(){};document.onreadystatechange=function(b){e(b);'loading'!==document.readyState&&(document.onreadystatechange=e,c())}}}})();</script></body></html>",,1177,http,200,ok,,2026-09-09 01:16:48.530049+03,2026-09-09 01:16:48.530049+03,2026-06-03 00:10:27.275024+03,ARM,AI Compute Silicon & Semiconductor IP,,,,,48.88,-0.014609845947756273,0.002506478609966445,-0.00011882756799574956,2026-09-09 02:24:39.088471+03,"these are the insights related to the article ""2 Top Semiconductor Stocks to Buy Before Artificial Intelligence (AI) Sends Them Soaring | The Motley Fool"" from The Motley Fool
- Semiconductor stocks have declined due to trade war concerns and risk-off sentiment, creating potential buying opportunities at attractive valuations, especially with AI as a growth driver.
- Marvell Technology's stock has fallen significantly, but its guidance for Q1 FY25 indicates a strong acceleration in growth, driven by custom AI processors and networking chips, making it an attractive buy.
- Marvell is well-positioned in the growing custom AI chip market, with increasing customer adoption and plans for next-generation 2nm chips, which could significantly boost AI revenue and market share.
- Arm Holdings' stock has also pulled back, making its valuation slightly more attractive. The company plays a crucial role in the AI chip market through its IP licensing, particularly for AI-focused architectures, which is driving strong royalty growth.
- Arm Holdings benefits from strong royalty revenue growth, especially from its AI-focused Armv9 architecture, which is contributing to significant earnings increases and is expected to accelerate due to the proliferation of AI.",validation,0.0035021158616663772,0.00494401628617136,MRVL,ARM,f,f,,0.003939880344374647,0.0010562450488513786,-0.0024068071312803863,f,0.004505813953488369,-0.00043604651162787444,market speculation,"The article is speculative, discussing potential future stock performance based on AI trends and market conditions, rather than reporting a concrete, newly-occurring event.",f,market speculation,"The article discusses potential future stock performance based on AI trends and provides buy recommendations, which is speculative rather than reporting a concrete event.",f,5
404,https://www.fool.com/investing/2024/11/12/what-nvidia-stock-investors-should-know-about-rece/?source=iedfolrf0000001,https://www.fool.com/investing/2024/11/12/what-nvidia-stock-investors-should-know-about-rece,fool.com,The Motley Fool,{NVDA},2024-11-12 17:15:00+02,What Nvidia Stock Investors Should Know About Recent Updates | The Motley Fool,Jose Najarro,"In today's video, I discuss recent updates affecting Nvidia (NVDA 0.84%). To learn more, check out the short video, consider subscribing, and click the special offer link below.
