- Striim has launched SQL2Fabric-X, a new solution for real-time data streaming and integration, enabling customers to replicate SQL Server databases to Microsoft Fabric and Azure Databricks. This product aims to provide fresher data for AI and analytics, with flexible pricing starting at $1500/monthly and a 30-day free trial available.
- Striim highlights its ongoing strategic partnership with Microsoft, building on a previous announcement at Ignite 2024. The general availability of SQL2Fabric-X expands on the initial public preview, offering broader capabilities and positive feedback from early customers interested in integrating on-premise SQL Server data with Azure Databricks.",validation,-0.004818339216449474,-0.00453147758536987,MSFT,MSFT,f,f,,-0.004965976351215429,0.00085034965034958,0.0009375585974125134,f,-0.004383775982302995,0.00014837395632416595,news-event,"The article announces the general availability of a new product, SQL2Fabric-X, which is a concrete, newly-occurring corporate event.",t,news-event,"The article reports on the general availability of a new product (SQL2Fabric-X) by Striim, which is a concrete, newly-occurring corporate event.",t,4
